<div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim</div>
<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Devarim HaNohagin B'Seudah — Halachah 4<br><span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:400;">Part 1: §§ 1–12 — Rosh HaShanah through Sukkos</span></div>
<div class="lm-subtitle">Based on <span class="v">"Tisha Tikkunin Yakirin"</span> <span class="sr">(<span class="lr">LM I, 20</span>)</span><br>Herein is explained the mystical dimension of Rosh HaShanah, Yom Kippur, the Ten Days of Teshuvah, Sukkos, the Four Species, Hoshana Rabbah, Shemini Atzeres, and Simchas Torah.</div>

<!-- §1 -->
<div class="sn">§ 1 — Rosh HaShanah: Revealing the Holiness of <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">All our service during these holy days — from Rosh HaShanah through the ten days of <span class="h">teshuvah</span>, <span class="h">erev</span> Yom Kippur, Yom Kippur itself, Sukkos, the four species, through Shemini Atzeres — is to <span class="kc">reveal the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span></span>, so that we merit to come there. <span class="h">Rabbainu</span> said when he taught this awesome Torah: <span class="mx">"Whoever wants to be a true Jew — to ascend from level to level — it is impossible except through <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>."</span> He also said: <span class="mx">"The main thing is when one merits to win the battle and come to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>"</span> — then one is called <span class="mx">"a mighty warrior."</span> Before arriving at <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"let not the one girding boast like the one removing."</span></div>

<div class="p">The holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed on Rosh HaShanah: <span class="v">"the eyes of Hashem your G-d are always upon it, from the beginning of the year to the end of the year."</span> In the Arizal's <span class="h">kavanos</span>: on Rosh HaShanah the <span class="h">nesirah</span> [cutting/separation] of <span class="h">Malchus</span> begins, continuing until Yom Kippur. In the four days between Yom Kippur and Sukkos, inner and surrounding <span class="h">chasadim</span> are drawn. On Shemini Atzeres, <span class="h">Knesses Yisrael</span> (= <span class="h">Malchus</span>) unites with her Beloved in love — the essential joy of Israel. All of this is the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, for <span class="h">Malchus</span> = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> = <span class="v">"a woman who fears Hashem."</span></div>

<div class="p">The essence of <span class="h">Malchus</span> is to reveal His kingship to all: <span class="v">"and so, place Your fear, Hashem our G-d, upon all Your works… rule over the entire world in Your glory… let every creature know that You formed it."</span> We conclude: <span class="v">"King over the whole earth, the holy King, the King of judgment."</span> All this = revealing <span class="h">Malchus</span> = revealing <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>'s holiness. For His kingship is primarily revealed there — Yerushalayim and the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>: <span class="v">"great is Hashem, and greatly praised, in the city of our G-d."</span> <span class="mx">"Whoever dwells in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is like one who has a G-d; whoever dwells outside — like one who has none."</span> On Rosh HaShanah eve we say <span class="v">"Mizmor L'Dovid — the earth is Hashem's"</span> — beginning with the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> (as Rashi explains), and ending with: <span class="v">"the King of glory shall enter."</span></div>

<!-- §2 -->
<div class="sn">§ 2 — Drawing Torah Through Mercy: Moshe's Error at the Rock</div>

<div class="p">To reveal <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>'s holiness, one must draw Torah — and one merits <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> through the Torah one draws. But one cannot enter until the <span class="kc">obstructers — the slanderers of the Land</span> — are subdued. Their subjugation depends on the renewal of Torah; the renewal of Torah depends on the additional holiness above.</div>

<div class="p">The essential principle from <span class="lr">LM I, 20</span>: <span class="kc">One who wishes to draw illuminations of Torah must pour out his prayer before Hashem in supplication.</span> Before the teaching, he must pray as a pauper begging for a free gift — not relying on his own merit. Though his <span class="h">mateh oz</span> [staff of strength from his good deeds] is aroused, it is not for self-glorification but for subduing the evil among the assembly. Before Hashem himself, he stands as a poor beggar, relying only on <span class="h">rachamim</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="kc">This was Moshe's error.</span> Hashem told him: "Take the staff" — to take the power of his merit for <span class="kc">subduing the evil among the assembly</span>. Then: "Speak to the rock" — speak gently, pour out prayer as a pauper. "Before their eyes" — connect with the souls of the assembly during the act. But Moshe used his staff's power for the Torah itself — drawing Torah by force, not through mercy and supplication, not connecting with the souls. Therefore the angels born from that Torah could not receive power from Edom [Esav's spiritual force] to subdue the obstructers. Edom answered: <span class="v">"you shall not pass through me."</span> Moshe could not enter <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Through his passing, Moshe's soul added holiness above — rectifying what was lacking. This entire teaching is explained in <span class="lr">LM I, 20</span>.</div>

<!-- §3 -->
<div class="sn">§ 3 — Rosh HaShanah: The Time of Gathering, Drawing Torah for <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">This is what we work to rectify on Rosh HaShanah — the time of gathering for all Israel, assembling around the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>. We draw Torah to reveal <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. The <span class="h">tzadikim</span> teach Torah on Rosh HaShanah; those gathered where no <span class="h">tzadik</span> teaches draw the Torah's holiness through the <span class="h">shofar</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">Matan Torah</span> given with the <span class="h">shofar</span>'s voice. We say: <span class="v">"You were revealed…"</span> — recalling <span class="h">Matan Torah</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">shenah</span> [sleep/dormita] in the <span class="h">kavanos</span> = removal of the <span class="h">mochin</span> so the <span class="h">Malchus</span> can be "sawed off" and rebuilt. This means <span class="kc">removing one's own merit</span> — standing before Hashem without relying on one's good deeds, empty-handed. <span class="mx">"There is no poor man except in <span class="h">da'as</span>"</span> — we remove our <span class="h">da'as</span>, standing as paupers. This is what we say at the beginning of <span class="h">Selichos</span>: <span class="v">"Yours, Hashem, is the righteousness, and ours the shame… not with merit or with deeds have we come before You — as paupers and beggars we knock at Your doors, for upon Your abundant mercies we trust."</span></div>

<div class="p">Even the true <span class="h">tzadik</span> with genuine merit does not use it for drawing Torah — he stands as a pauper requesting free gifts of mercy. The <span class="h">Shaliach Tzibbur</span> begins: <span class="v">"Hineni he'ani mima'as"</span> — "Here I am, impoverished of deeds." The <span class="h">tzadik</span> directs his <span class="h">Gevuros</span> (= <span class="h">mateh oz</span>) toward <span class="h">Malchus</span> (= <span class="h">Knesses Yisrael</span>) to subdue the evil, while receiving <span class="h">Chasadim</span> for himself — requesting only free grace. Through this precisely, <span class="h">Malchus</span> is sawed off and rebuilt = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is established.</div>

<!-- §4 -->
<div class="sn">§ 4 — The <i>Shofar</i>: Awakening from Sleep, Drawing New <i>Mochin</i></div>

<div class="p">Then comes the <span class="h">shofar</span> — awakening from the sleep. New <span class="h">mochin</span> are drawn = Torah illuminations = Torah innovations. <span class="h">Shofar</span> = <span class="h">Matan Torah</span> given with the <span class="h">shofar</span>'s voice. Then hot words like fiery coals are drawn — through which Torah illuminations flow. <span class="h">Shofar</span> = <span class="h">yirah</span> = fire: <span class="v">"the people saw the sounds and the flames and the voice of the <span class="h">shofar</span>"</span>; <span class="v">"His words you heard from amid the fire."</span> Only one whose words are like fiery coals can draw Torah illuminations — as at <span class="h">Sinai</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is merited through the abundant mercy and supplication throughout <span class="h">Selichos</span>, Rosh HaShanah itself, and especially before the <span class="h">shofar</span> — when all Israel break their hearts deeply, crying as paupers. Through this, the new <span class="h">mochin</span> come via the <span class="h">shofar</span>. Through the renewal of <span class="h">mochin</span> = Torah illuminations, we merit <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, and the building of <span class="h">Malchus</span> begins.</div>

<!-- §5 -->
<div class="sn">§ 5 — <i>Malchiyos, Zichronos, Shofaros</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="kc">All three are aspects of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>.</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Malchiyos</span> = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: the primary revelation of His kingship is there. We begin with <span class="v">"Aleinu L'Shabei'ach"</span> — that wondrous praise through which Yehoshua and Israel conquered Yericho (the gateway to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>). They said <span class="h">Aleinu</span> and blew <span class="h">shofaros</span>. We do the same on Rosh HaShanah: after the <span class="h">shofar</span>, we say <span class="h">Aleinu</span> to open <span class="h">Malchiyos</span> — conquering <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> through praise.</div>

<!-- §6 -->
<div class="sn">§ 6 — <i>Zichronos</i>: The Name, Memory, and <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Zichronos</span> = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"and the Land I will remember."</span> Rosh HaShanah is called <span class="h">Yom HaZikaron</span> [Day of Remembrance]. <span class="h">Zikaron</span> = <span class="h">shem</span> [name]: <span class="v">"this is My Name forever, and this is My remembrance for all generations."</span> The <span class="h">shem</span> of every creature is its remembrance — through the name one recalls the thing's entire essence. When one mentions "table" or "ox" — the entire form is understood. Similarly, mentioning a person's name encompasses his entire being. And Hashem's Name = His remembrance: we can only refer to Him through His holy Names.</div>

<div class="p">The essential remembrance of His Name is in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — in the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> where the explicit Name is pronounced: <span class="v">"in every place where I cause My Name to be remembered, I will come to you and bless you."</span> <span class="v">"Known in Yehudah is G-d; in Israel, great is His Name."</span> The holiness radiates from the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> throughout <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>'s borders.</div>

<div class="p">When Avraham entered <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"Avraham called there in the Name of Hashem."</span> Through meriting <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, his name was enlarged with a <span class="h">hei</span>. <span class="v">"Your name shall no longer be Avram… and I will give you the land."</span> Name = <span class="h">Malchus</span> = Land = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Just as the earth is the furthest extent of materiality, so His Name is the furthest "descent" from His unfathomable greatness into revelation.</div>

<div class="p">The essential judgment on Rosh HaShanah examines one's <span class="h">shem</span> — all deeds are inscribed there. <span class="v">"A living soul — that is its name."</span> The <span class="h">shem</span> = <span class="h">nefesh</span> = life-force. Eating blemishes or rectifies the <span class="h">shem</span>: <span class="v">"you shall eat and be satisfied, and praise the Name of Hashem."</span> The rectification of eating = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Therefore <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> commands: <span class="v">"bless Hashem your G-d for the Land."</span></div>

<!-- §7 -->
<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>Shofaros</i>: Ingathering of Exiles to <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Shofaros</span> = ingathering of exiles: <span class="v">"on that day a great <span class="h">shofar</span> shall be blown, and the lost in Ashur and the dispersed in Mitzrayim shall come and bow to Hashem on the holy mountain in Yerushalayim."</span> After the <span class="h">Shofaros</span> verses: <span class="v">"blow the great <span class="h">shofar</span> for our freedom… gather our exiles… bring us to Tziyon Your city in song."</span></div>

<div class="p">All three — <span class="h">Malchiyos</span>, <span class="h">Zichronos</span>, <span class="h">Shofaros</span> — are <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. The <span class="h">shofar</span> is not merely instrumental but = <span class="h">Matan Torah</span> = Torah drawn through mercy and supplication = subjugation of obstructers = path to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Moshe is <span class="h">Mashiach</span> — he will return and rectify the error at the rock, drawing Torah through mercy, returning all Israel in <span class="h">teshuvah</span>, and bringing everyone to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<!-- §8 -->
<div class="sn">§ 8 — The Ten Days: Ten Levels of Holiness in <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">The ten days from Rosh HaShanah to Yom Kippur = the ten levels of holiness in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> (Mishnah <span class="h">Keilim</span> 1:6). In each day, new <span class="h">mochin</span> are drawn through <span class="h">teshuvah</span>, building <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> (= <span class="h">Malchus</span>) further. On Yom Kippur — the tenth day — we reach the tenth and highest holiness: <span class="h">Kodesh HaKodashim</span>. The <span class="h">Kohein Gadol</span> enters there on that day alone — for then we merit the supreme holiness.</div>

<!-- §9 -->
<div class="sn">§ 9 — <i>Sukkah</i>: The Path to <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">On Sukkos, we conquer <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> through the four species — <span class="mx">"weapons of war"</span> (Zohar). Through Rosh HaShanah and the ten days, we drew Torah via <span class="h">teshuvah</span> and prayer; now we fight the obstructers to enter the Land. The <span class="h">sukkah</span> = Clouds of Glory = the road to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"Hashem went before them by day in a pillar of cloud, to guide them on the way."</span> The Clouds smoothed the path, killed snakes and scorpions, and subdued Amalek. All obstacles on the journey = snakes, scorpions, Amalek — subdued through the Clouds = the <span class="h">sukkah</span>.</div>

<!-- §10 -->
<div class="sn">§ 10 — <i>Sukkos</i>: Conquering the Land</div>

<div class="p">On Sukkos we conquer <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Rosh HaShanah and Yom Kippur built and revealed the holiness; now we must enter. We fight the obstructers — the slanderers of the Land — to arrive at <span class="h">Malchus</span> on Shemini Atzeres, when <span class="h">Malchus</span> is perfected and united with her Beloved = the perfection of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<!-- §11 -->
<div class="sn">§ 11 — The Four Species: Weapons of War</div>

<div class="p">The four species = <span class="mx">"<span class="h">mana krava</span>"</span> [weapons of war] (Zohar): <span class="mx">"who is victorious? He who holds weapons in his hands."</span> Through Torah innovations, angels are created who receive power from Edom to punish the obstructers. The four species = this power received from Edom to subdue those blocking <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. The Zohar: the four species show we <span class="kc">won the battle on Rosh HaShanah</span> — through Torah drawn properly, we merited the weapons.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">esrog</span> = <span class="h">Malchus</span> = <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> = <span class="v">"you are entirely beautiful, my beloved, and there is no blemish in you"</span> = <span class="v">"a woman who fears Hashem."</span> The <span class="h">esrog</span> must be flawless — for we are uprooting the slander against the Land. Through taking a beautiful <span class="h">esrog</span> without blemish, the beauty of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed: <span class="v">"you will lack nothing in it."</span></div>

<!-- §12 -->
<div class="sn">§ 12 — <i>Lulav</i>, <i>Hadas</i>, <i>Aravah</i>: The <i>Tzadik</i>'s Weapons</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Lulav</span> = <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> shall flourish like a palm tree"</span> = the <span class="h">tzadik</span> who guards the <span class="h">bris</span> = <span class="v">"gird your sword upon your thigh."</span> The <span class="h">tzadik</span>'s weapons come through <span class="h">tikkun habris</span> — enabling him to draw Torah and receive power to subdue the obstructers.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Aravos</span> [willows] = the wicked and sinners of Israel. The <span class="h">tzadik</span> binds himself with them, subduing their evil and returning them in <span class="h">teshuvah</span>. Through this he draws Torah in great abundance: <span class="v">"He opened the rock and waters flowed."</span> The more souls he rectifies, the more holiness above, the more Torah flows. The <span class="h">aravah</span> grows by water — hinting that the <span class="h">tikkun</span> of the wicked is through <span class="v">"pouring out your heart like water before Hashem"</span> = abundant mercy and supplication.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Hadas</span> [myrtle] = beautiful fragrance but bitter taste = the <span class="h">neshamah</span> that suffers the bitterness of Torah's yoke. The <span class="h">neshamah</span> = <span class="h">reiach</span> [scent]: <span class="mx">"what gives pleasure to the <span class="h">neshamah</span> but not the body? Fragrance."</span> The <span class="h">hadas</span> is tripled — for the Torah itself is triple: <span class="mx">"Blessed is the Merciful One who gave a threefold Torah."</span> The <span class="h">neshamah</span> despises worldly pleasures, living only for the <span class="h">reiach</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Thus: <span class="h">lulav</span> + <span class="h">hadas</span> + <span class="h">aravah</span> = the <span class="h">tzadik</span> draws weapons from the <span class="h">neshamah</span>'s Torah (= <span class="h">hadas</span>), through returning the wicked (= <span class="h">aravah</span>) via pouring out prayer like water, drawing Torah in great flow. All this warfare — to conquer <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> (= the <span class="h">esrog</span> joined with the three species). The <span class="h">na'anu'im</span> [wavings] = arousing the mind to draw <span class="h">mochin</span> into the <span class="h">esrog</span>.</div>

<div class="p">On Sukkos, we receive power from Edom itself to subdue obstructers — therefore the seventy bulls are offered for the seventy nations. We need their power to uphold the holy <span class="h">das</span> [religion]. Through the sacrifices, the good hidden among the nations (= holy judgment that fell among them) is extracted and returned to us.</div>

<!-- Translator's Summary Part 1 -->
<div class="ts">
  <div class="sh">✦ Translator's Summary — Part 1 (§§ 1–12) ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;">This massive <em>halachah</em> — based on <strong>LM I:20</strong> (<em>Tisha Tikkunin</em>) — maps the entire cycle of <em>Tishrei</em> onto a single spiritual drama: <strong>revealing and conquering <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>.</strong></p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>The Core Teaching</strong>: To reach <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>, one must draw Torah — but only through mercy and supplication, never through the "staff of strength" of one's own merit. Moshe's error at the rock was using his merit to draw Torah by force instead of through humble prayer connected to the assembly's souls. This prevented his entry into the Land. Through his passing, he rectified this — and as <em>Mashiach</em>, he will return to draw Torah properly and bring everyone to <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>The Tishrei Cycle</strong>:<br>
  • <strong>Rosh HaShanah</strong> (§§1-4): Removing one's own <em>mochin</em> (= sleep/dormita), standing as a pauper. Then the <em>shofar</em> awakens new <em>mochin</em> = Torah illuminations = fire. <em>Malchiyos</em>, <em>Zichronos</em>, <em>Shofaros</em> (§§5-7) — all three = <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>.<br>
  • <strong>Ten Days</strong> (§8): Ten levels of holiness. Yom Kippur = <em>Kodesh HaKodashim</em>, the tenth and highest.<br>
  • <strong>Sukkos</strong> (§§9-12): Now we conquer. The <em>sukkah</em> = Clouds of Glory = the road. The four species = weapons of war. <em>Esrog</em> = <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> (flawless). <em>Lulav</em> = the <em>tzadik</em>. <em>Aravah</em> = wicked returned through mercy. <em>Hadas</em> = the <em>neshamah</em>'s Torah. Seventy bulls for seventy nations — extracting holy judgment from among them.</p>

  <p style="font-style:italic;">Part 2 continues with §§13-23: Ushpizin, Hoshana Rabbah, Shemini Atzeres, and the application to eating and bread.</p>
